---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { PANTRYBABY_SUPPORT_EMAIL, PRIVACY_EMAIL } from '../../data/pantrybaby';
import { COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME, COMPANY_DBA, GOVERNING_LAW_STATE } from '../../data/legal';

const lastUpdated = 'October 20, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="PantryBaby Terms of Use"
  description="PantryBaby Terms of Use: acceptable use, auto-renewing subscriptions and free trials, food-safety notice, limitations, and contact information."
  canonical="/pantrybaby/terms"
  theme="pantry"
  product="pantrybaby"
>
  <div class="policy-layout">
    <div class="container-sm">
      <div class="policy-header">
        <a href="/pantrybaby" class="policy-back">← PantryBaby</a>
        <div class="label-chip" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">Legal</div>
        <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
        <p class="policy-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated} · Applies to PantryBaby for iOS</p>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-summary glass">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>PantryBaby is a personal pantry, shopping list and expiry reminder app for your household.</li>
          <li>Premium is an auto-renewing subscription billed by Apple. A free trial, if offered, turns into a paid subscription unless you cancel at least 24 hours before it ends.</li>
          <li>Manage or cancel Premium in your Apple ID settings. Deleting the app or your data does not cancel it.</li>
          <li>Expiry dates and "Use It Up" suggestions are reminders, not food-safety advice. Always check the food itself.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="policy-content">

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>1. About PantryBaby</h2>
          <p>
            PantryBaby is a personal pantry and grocery list app published by <strong>{COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME}</strong>,
            operating as {COMPANY_DBA} ("we," "us," "our"). The app is available for iPhone on iOS 17.0 and later.
          </p>
          <p>
            PantryBaby helps you keep track of what is in your kitchen, what is running low, what to buy, and
            what to use before it expires. It is not a nutrition, dietary, medical, or food-safety service, and
            nothing in the app or on this site is professional advice.
          </p>
          <p>
            PantryBaby is part of the BabyBlocks family of apps. If you create an account, it is a BabyBlocks
            account that also works with our other apps, such as BudgetBaby. See the
            <a href="/pantrybaby/privacy#shared-account">Privacy Policy</a> for what that means for your data.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>2. Acceptable use</h2>
          <p>You may use PantryBaby for your personal and household, non-commercial use. You agree not to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the app, except where the law allows it.</li>
            <li>Use the app in any unlawful manner or for any unlawful purpose.</li>
            <li>Attempt to circumvent or disable any security features, including Premium access controls.</li>
            <li>Share your account credentials with others or allow others to sign in to your account.</li>
            <li>Use the app to provide a service to others, or to process other people's data as a business, without our written consent.</li>
            <li>Send abusive, unlawful, or misleading content through support tickets or feature requests.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>3. Food-safety notice</h2>
          <p>
            PantryBaby shows expiry dates that you enter, reminders based on those dates, and suggestions such as
            "Use It Up" that point at items you may want to use soon. These are reminders to help you plan. They
            are not food-safety advice.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>A date in PantryBaby is only as accurate as what was entered. It is not a guarantee that food is safe, or unsafe, to eat.</li>
            <li>Always check the food itself, its packaging and its storage instructions, and follow official food-safety guidance where you live.</li>
            <li>PantryBaby does not know about allergies, recalls, or how an item has been stored, and its suggestions do not account for them.</li>
            <li>A missed, late, or incorrect reminder (for example, because notifications are turned off) is not a statement that food is safe.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>4. Subscriptions and free trials</h2>

          <h3>PantryBaby Premium</h3>
          <p>
            PantryBaby Premium is an optional, auto-renewing subscription, offered monthly or annually and
            purchased through the Apple App Store. The price, billing period, and any introductory offer are
            shown in the app and on the App Store purchase sheet before you confirm. The price you see there,
            in your local currency, is the price you pay. Prices can differ by country and can change; a price
            change does not affect a period you have already paid for, and Apple tells you before a higher price
            applies to a renewal.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Auto-renewal.</strong> Your subscription renews automatically at the end of each period, at the then-current price, unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the current period ends.</li>
            <li><strong>Billing.</strong> Payment is charged to your Apple ID account when you confirm the purchase, or, if you start a free trial, when the trial ends. Renewals are charged within the 24 hours before the current period ends.</li>
            <li><strong>Manage or cancel.</strong> Open the iOS Settings app, tap your name, then Subscriptions, then PantryBaby. You can also reach this from PantryBaby's subscription screen. Cancelling stops the next renewal; you keep Premium until the end of the period you have paid for.</li>
            <li><strong>Deleting is not cancelling.</strong> Deleting PantryBaby, deleting your PantryBaby data, or deleting your BabyBlocks account does not cancel an Apple subscription. It keeps renewing until you cancel it in your Apple ID settings.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Free trials</h3>
          <p>
            We may offer a free trial of Premium, for example a 7-day free trial. Whether a trial is offered, and
            how long it lasts, is shown before you confirm.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>When the trial ends, it converts automatically to a paid subscription at the price shown, unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the trial ends.</li>
            <li>If you buy a subscription during a free trial, any unused portion of the trial is forfeited when the purchase takes effect.</li>
            <li>Free trials are generally limited to one per Apple ID, as determined by Apple.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Paid introductory offers</h3>
          <p>
            We may also offer a paid introductory price, for example a reduced price for the first period, or a
            single up-front payment for an introductory period. The offer's price, length, and what you pay
            afterwards are shown before you confirm. When the introductory period ends, the subscription renews
            at the regular price unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the introductory period ends.
          </p>

          <h3>Free features</h3>
          <p>
            You can use PantryBaby's core pantry and shopping list features without paying. The free limits are
            shown in the app. We may adjust free limits or which features are Premium with reasonable notice, and
            we will not take away Premium features you have already paid for within a current billing period.
          </p>

          <h3>Refunds</h3>
          <p>
            Purchases are processed by Apple, and Apple decides refunds. Request one at
            <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
            We cannot issue refunds for App Store purchases ourselves.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>5. Accounts</h2>
          <p>
            You can use PantryBaby without an account. Signing in (with Apple, Google, or an email and password)
            is needed for cloud sync and cloud backup. You are responsible for keeping your sign-in details secure
            and for activity on your account.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your BabyBlocks account is shared across BabyBlocks apps. Deleting it from PantryBaby deletes it for
            BudgetBaby too. PantryBaby offers a separate option that deletes only PantryBaby's data and keeps your
            account. See <a href="/pantrybaby/delete-data">Delete your data</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>6. Your data</h2>
          <p>
            You own the content you put into PantryBaby: your items, lists, stores, notes, and photos. We do not
            claim ownership of it. You give us only the permission we need to store, sync, and back it up for you
            when you use those features, and to look at what you send us when you ask for support.
          </p>
          <p>
            How we handle your data is described in our <a href="/pantrybaby/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Please keep your own backups of anything important. We are not liable for data loss caused by device
            failure, uninstalling the app, a lost encryption key, or other circumstances outside our reasonable
            control.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>7. Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p>
            PantryBaby is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, either express or implied,
            to the maximum extent permitted by law. We do not warrant that the app will be uninterrupted, error-free,
            or that reminders and suggestions will always be accurate or on time.
          </p>
          <p>
            To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, {COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME} is not liable for:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Illness, injury, or loss arising from eating, using, keeping, or throwing away food or household items, including decisions based on dates, reminders, or suggestions shown in the app.</li>
            <li>Shopping, spending, or household decisions made based on information in the app.</li>
            <li>Loss of data due to device failure, app bugs, or user error.</li>
            <li>Any indirect, incidental, special, or consequential damages arising from your use of the app.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Some places do not allow some of these limitations, so they may not all apply to you. Nothing in these
            Terms limits rights you have under consumer law that cannot be waived.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>8. Intellectual property</h2>
          <p>
            PantryBaby, including its design, code, and content, is owned by {COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME}.
            All rights reserved. The BabyBlocks and PantryBaby names and related marks are trademarks of {COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME}.
          </p>
          <p>
            Nothing in these Terms grants you any right to use our trademarks, logos, or brand assets
            without prior written consent.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>9. Apple</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms are between you and {COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME}, not Apple. Apple is not responsible for PantryBaby
            or its content, has no obligation to provide maintenance or support for it, and is not responsible for
            any claims relating to it. Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and
            may enforce them against you. Your use of the app must also follow the App Store's
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Usage Rules</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>10. Changes to the app and terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update PantryBaby and these Terms from time to time. We will tell you about material changes to
            these Terms in the app or on this page, and update the "last updated" date. Your continued use after a
            change takes effect means you accept it.
          </p>
          <p>
            We may add, change, or remove features. We will not retroactively take away Premium features you have
            already paid for within a current billing period.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of {GOVERNING_LAW_STATE}, United States, without regard to
            conflict of law principles, except where the law of the place you live requires otherwise.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="policy-section">
          <h2>12. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about these Terms? Email us at <a href={`mailto:${PANTRYBABY_SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{PANTRYBABY_SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
            or <a href="mailto:support@babyblocks.io">support@babyblocks.io</a>. For privacy requests, email
            <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.<br />
            <strong>{COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME}</strong> · operating as {COMPANY_DBA}
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy-layout {
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + var(--space-12));
    padding-bottom: var(--space-24);
  }

  .policy-back {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-block;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .policy-back:hover { color: var(--text-secondary); }

  .policy-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
  }

  .policy-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-3xl), 5vw, var(--text-5xl));
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .policy-meta {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy-summary {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  .policy-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-10);
  }

  .policy-section h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .policy-section h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .policy-section p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .policy-section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .policy-section ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-block: var(--space-3);
  }
</style>
